<!--
	PrimeFaces SAIL conformance for converters: date times and timestamps shown as dates (kitchensink.ConvertersFixture, an attribute per converter).
	Records a, b and c are entered in each field and in an inline grid row, typed as a user types them, then checked
	with testValue after the save and once reopened from the list. Then each column is filtered in the Vue list grid
	(the list view) and in the PrimeFaces data table (ConvertersDataTables), with values written as the cells show
	them, and the rows each filter leaves are checked. The values catch day and month swapped, 12 hour times at PM,
	noon and midnight, month names, seconds, negatives, separators, $ and percentages, and rounding.
	Run by PrimeFacesConvertersSailIT.
-->
